  "id": "explicit-memory",
  "term": "explicit memory",
  "definition": "Explicit memory is memory that depends on conscious recall or deliberate learning. It includes memory-related functions that involve actively searching short-term or long-term memory, such as short-term and working memory, although it overlaps to some extent with implicit memory rather than being completely separate from it.",
